{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And HaShem turned a sea wind.</b> The west is called \"sea\" in the holy language, because of the great sea that goes out from Spain and passes by the land of Egypt, to the land of Israel, and it is on the western side and is not the Ocean sea, for Israel did not inherit that far. And the sea of Spain is called \"the great sea\" because its width is three hundred parasangs, and the other seas in the land of Israel—the Sea of Reeds, the Sea of Kinneret, and the Salt Sea—have none whose width is thirty parasangs."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:13.758346207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}